131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 321 0 R
/E (Overview of Related Work: Previous studies in news classification have largely focused on simpler binary or single-label classifications, such as detecting misinformation on social media or categorizing news by general themes. These approaches fall short in addressing the complexity of classifying news into multiple ministerial domains.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 322 0 R
/E (Positioning DemocraticNet: By adapting state-of-the-art transformer models specifically for multi-label classification tasks, DemocraticNet moves beyond previous studies to tackle the unique challenges of government news classification.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Novelty and Contribution: DemocraticNet pioneers a system optimized for categorizing news articles relevant to government ministries. Unlike existing systems, it can handle cross-ministerial classifications in real-time, making it a novel and essential tool for governmental communication and misinformation management.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
